Note: What is the difference between array and vector? 
There is everything almost same only the difference is size, vector size is dyanamic/flexible and array is fixed(no change can be done).

1. size() --> no. of elements store
2. capacity() --> no. of elements it can store
3. push_back() --> append new element inside the vector
4. pop_back() --> delete last element of the vector
5. emplace_back() --> append new elemnts inside the vector

Both push_back() and emplace_back() acts like same but they are little bit different, push_back() thinks it will get the same datatype elements but emblace_back() creats emblace object.

6. at() or [] --> to get any position elements like 0 1 2 3 4 .........
7. front() --> get the first element
8. back()  --> get the last element

// new page
9. erase() --> we pass to iterators to erase elements of the vector by change it size but not the capacity

10. insert() --> inserting new elemetn in the vector

11. clear() --> totally clearing all the elements of the vector

12. empty() --> checking if the vector is empty


